  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through Wednesday) \nIssued at 113 AM MST Thu Nov 19 2026\n\nQuasi-zonal flow will develop Sunday into Monday across New Mexico, \nmoderating temperatures back up to within a few degrees of seasonal \naverages. The overall weather pattern looks to become more \nprogressive again mid to late next week as a potent Pacific jet \ndevelops over the eastern Pacific. This will increase the chance \nthat additional quick-hitting storm systems impact New Mexico. The \ncurrent forecast shows low rain/mountain snow chances Tuesday and \nthen again Thursday, but the timing of these quick-hitting troughs \nwill likely change in the coming days considering the high \ndisagreement among ensemble systems. Temperatures will likely hover \nnear seasonal normals, potentially dropping below normal behind \nfrequent Pacific frontal passages.",
